> [After] the martyrdom of St. Boniface, Verg[ili]us was made Bishop of[ Sal]zburg (766 or 7[67]) and laboured successfully[ for] the upbuilding of his[ di]ocese as well as for the spread of the Faith in neighbouring heat[hen] countries[,] especially in Carinthia. He died at Salzburg, 27 November, 789. In 1233 he was canonized by Gregory IX. His doctrine that the earth is a sphere was derived from the[ teaching] of[ ancient] geographers[,] and his belief in the existence of the antipodes was probably influenced by the accounts which the[ ancient Irish] voyagers gave of[ their] journeys. This, at least, is the opinion of Rettberg ("Kirchengesch.[ De]utschlands", II[,] 236).[][][]

